Vertex at $x - 2 = 0 \implies x = 2$, so vertex is $(2,0)$.
$y$-intercept at $x = 0$: $y = |0 - 2| = 2$, so $(0,2)$.
Symmetric V-shape opening upwards with axis of symmetry $x = 2$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-2.5,0) -- (5.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1) -- (0,5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <->] (-2,4) -- (2,0) -- (5,3);
\fill (2,0) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (0,2) circle (2pt);
\node[font=\small] at (4,3.8) {$y=|x-2|$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

