mastery.question_text:
The diagram below shows the inverted graph $f(x) = -|ax + b|$ with vertex $(4,0)$ and $y$-intercept $(0,-8)$.
Find the equation of $f(x)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-1.5,0) -- (7.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-9.5) -- (0,2) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-1,1,2,3,4,5,6,7} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[above,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {-8,-6,-4,-2} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <->] (-0.5,-9) -- (4,0) -- (7,-6);
\fill (4,0) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (0,-8) circle (2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.solution_text:
The denominator cannot be zero, so $x \ne 1$. Domain is $(-\infty, 1) \cup (1, \infty)$.
For $x > 1$, $x - 1 > 0 \implies |x - 1| = x - 1 \implies f(x) = \frac{x - 1}{x - 1} = 1$.
For $x < 1$, $x - 1 < 0 \implies |x - 1| = -(x - 1) \implies f(x) = \frac{-(x - 1)}{x - 1} = -1$.
The graph consists of two horizontal rays with open circles at $(1,1)$ and $(1,-1)$.
$\text{Range} = \{-1, 1\}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-3.5,0) -- (4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.5) -- (0,2.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {-2,-1,1,2} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <-] (-3,-1) -- (1,-1);
\draw[thick, ->] (1,1) -- (4,1);
\draw[fill=white] (1,-1) circle (2.5pt);
\draw[fill=white] (1,1) circle (2.5pt);
\node[font=\small] at (3,1.6) {$y=1$};
\node[font=\small] at (-2,-1.6) {$y=-1$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For $x \ge 0$, $|x| = x \implies f(x) = x - x = 0$ (horizontal ray along positive $x$-axis).
For $x < 0$, $|x| = -x \implies f(x) = x - (-x) = 2x$ (line with slope $2$).
The two branches meet continuously at $(0,0)$.
$\text{Domain} = (-\infty, \infty)$
$\text{Range} = (-\infty, 0]$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\draw[->] (-3.5,0) -- (3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-4.5) -- (0,2.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-3,-2,-1,1,2,3} {\draw (\x,0.1) -- (\x,-0.1); \node[above,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0.1) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2} {\draw (0.1,\y) -- (-0.1,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[above left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick, <-] (-2,-4) -- (0,0);
\draw[thick, ->] (0,0) -- (3,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (2.5pt);
\node[font=\small] at (-1.5,-1.5) {$y=2x$};
\node[font=\small] at (2,0.5) {$y=0$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
